WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.926
Mrs. Desai is sixty-eight. This morning, a caller posing as her bank took one lakh twenty thousand rupees.

2
00:00:08.326 --> 00:00:12.924
I feel so ashamed. Please don't tell my son.

3
00:00:13.324 --> 00:00:22.445
Shame keeps most victims silent. So the first job is not the form. It is a calm voice. Farah uses CALM.

4
00:00:22.745 --> 00:00:30.181
C is for calm and connect. You did the right thing by telling me. We will handle this together.

5
00:00:30.481 --> 00:00:38.280
A: act on what is urgent. Is she safe? Then the golden-hour steps: nineteen thirty, and the bank.

6
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:45.607
L: listen and log. Facts only, with her consent. Never ask, why did you.

7
00:00:45.907 --> 00:00:52.245
M: map the next steps. Write them down, with the acknowledgement number and a follow-up date.

8
00:00:52.745 --> 00:01:00.145
Fraudsters are trained professionals, with scripts, psychology and AI. Being deceived is not foolishness.

9
00:01:00.545 --> 00:01:07.614
Adapt for each person. Senior citizens need patience, and the Elder Line: one four five six seven.

10
00:01:07.914 --> 00:01:16.016
Women: privacy, a female responder if possible, and never ask to see images. Helpline one eight one.

11
00:01:16.316 --> 00:01:23.521
Children: involve a parent or counsellor, and follow POCSO duties. Childline: ten ninety-eight.

12
00:01:23.921 --> 00:01:31.468
Serious distress? Stay with them, and connect them to Tele-MANAS, one four four one six, or one one two.

13
00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:38.888
Listen first. Act fast. Never blame. Safety before money, always.
